From ccc479e50501be0c433c16d03fb48a6268b58072 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:54:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] l5-pmus-live: a venue equity baseline, transfer
 detection, and the equity controls published for a second strategy

l5_equity_baseline (pure): an owner-written baseline record (venue buying
power, positions, zero open orders, timestamp, and the historical figures it
starts after, which are preserved); drawdown measured from it; a period
result that counts only rows with a measured cost and lists uncertain rows
beside it, added to nothing. Malformed is INVALID and refuses.

l5_equity_feed: a paced GET-only read of the activity feed for deposits,
transfers and bonuses since the baseline. Amounts are not interpreted: any
such row, an undated one, or a read the venue did not itself end (explicit
eof) is a refusal until the owner writes a new baseline. A gain adds no room.

Runner: the account risk record now also carries portfolio_drawdown and
equity_baseline, each with its own refusal, computed on a value withheld
when buying power is unread or older than 180s, order state is uncertain or
positions are unreadable. Added keys only. This service's own gates, the
ledger and every limit are unchanged; nothing is read unless a baseline
document is set.

98 new tests. Not deployed.

