From 56dfa0b7178ccf1ea6a43cd7a17d2b8cff5f2ed8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 01:12:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] l5-pmus-live: the transfer read is complete only when the
 venue ends the feed

The release commit before this one carried the earlier transfer check, which
stopped after two pages a day older than the baseline. The feed is not
strictly ordered, so that was an unmeasured assumption. It is removed: a
read counts only on the venue's explicit eof; a page with no cursor and no
eof, or MAX_PAGES, is INCOMPLETE and refuses. Full reads repeat every 15
minutes and go stale after 35.

The three tests for this were already in the previous commit and failed
there; they pass here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HTk927uH8zwpj6gLES92PF
---
 src/l5_equity_feed.py | 65 +++++++++++++++++++++----------------------
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

